+    <section>
+      <title><function moreinfo="none">assign_server(async_reply_route,
+      domain, direction, assignment_type)</function></title>
+
+      <para>Sends a Cx Server-Assignment-Request on behalf of a request other
+      than REGISTER, downloading the served user's profile into usrloc. The
+      transaction is suspended and resumed in async_reply_route once the SAA
+      arrives, with $avp(saa_return_code) set to 1 when a profile was stored
+      and to a negative value otherwise. No reply is sent by the module; that
+      is left to the route.</para>
+
+      <para>Meaning of the parameters is as follows:</para>
+
+      <itemizedlist>
+        <listitem>
+          <para><emphasis>async_reply_route</emphasis> - route to resume in
+          when the SAA arrives.</para>
+        </listitem>
+
+        <listitem>
+          <para><emphasis>domain</emphasis> - Logical domain within
+          registrar.</para>
+        </listitem>
+
+        <listitem>
+          <para><emphasis>direction</emphasis> - "orig" takes the served user
+          from the P-Asserted-Identity, "term" from the Request-URI.</para>
+        </listitem>
+
+        <listitem>
+          <para><emphasis>assignment_type</emphasis> - the
+          Server-Assignment-Type, an integer or a variable holding one:</para>
+
+          <itemizedlist>
+            <listitem>
+              <para>0 (NO_ASSIGNMENT) - fetch the profile without changing
+              anything at the HSS. The HSS answers DIAMETER_UNABLE_TO_COMPLY
+              when another S-CSCF is assigned to the user. An IMPU already in
+              usrloc keeps its registration state and bindings; a new one is
+              stored as unregistered. This is the S-CSCF restoration procedure
+              for an originating request (3GPP TS 23.380 4.4.2).</para>
+            </listitem>
+
+            <listitem>
+              <para>3 (UNREGISTERED_USER) - fetch the unregistered profile and
+              tell the HSS the user is unregistered here (3GPP TS 29.228
+              6.1.2.1).</para>
+            </listitem>
+          </itemizedlist>
+
+          <para>Any other type is refused: REGISTRATION and RE_REGISTRATION
+          are sent by save(), and the de-registration types would leave usrloc
+          out of step with the HSS.</para>
+        </listitem>
+      </itemizedlist>
+
+      <para>This function can be used in REQUEST_ROUTE.</para>
+
+      <example>
+        <title><function>assign_server</function> usage</title>
+
+        <programlisting format="linespecific">...
+assign_server("ORIG_SAA", "location", "orig", 0);
+...
+route[ORIG_SAA] {
+    if($avp(saa_return_code) != 1) {
+        t_reply("504", "Server Time-out");
+        exit;
+    }
+    # continue as for a registered user
+}
+...
+</programlisting>
+      </example>
+    </section>
+
